hadiths[50]{hadithnumber,text}:
"451","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both): We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) when an Ansari companion came, greeted the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) with salam, and then turned to leave. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked, ""O Ansari brother! How is my brother Sa'd?"" He replied, ""He is well."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Who among you will visit him?"" (Saying this) the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) stood up, and we also stood up with him. There were more people with us, and we had neither shoes, nor socks, nor caps, nor shirts (this was the height of the Companions' asceticism and their disinterest in the world), and we walked on that stony ground until we reached him. And those who were with Sayyiduna Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him) moved aside, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and those who came with him went to him."
"452","Umm al-Mu’minin Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you visit a sick person or a deceased person, say good words, because the angels say Ameen to what you say. She says that when Abu Salamah (may Allah be pleased with him) passed away, I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)! Abu Salamah has passed away. So he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pray like this: “O Allah! Forgive me and him, and grant me a better substitute than him.” She says that I made this supplication, so Allah Almighty granted me a better substitute than him, that is, Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"453","Abu Sa'id Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Instruct (encourage) your dying (those near death) to say ""La ilaha illallah"" (There is no god but Allah)."
"454","‘Mother of the Believers, Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Whoever wishes to meet Allah, Allah also wishes to meet him, and whoever does not wish to meet Allah, Allah does not wish to meet him. I said, “O Messenger of Allah! All of us dislike death.” So he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: That is not what I meant. Rather, when the believer’s final moment comes, he is given the glad tidings of Allah’s mercy, His pleasure, and Paradise, so he wishes to meet Allah (and desires to be quickly freed from illness and the distresses of the world), and Allah also wishes to meet him. And when the disbeliever’s final moment comes, he is informed of Allah’s punishment and His anger, so he does not wish to meet Allah, and Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, does not wish to meet him. In another narration, it is narrated from Shuraih bin Hani that Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Whoever wishes to meet Allah, Allah also wishes to meet him, and whoever dislikes to meet Allah, Allah also dislikes to meet him. After hearing this hadith from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him), I went to Mother of the Believers, Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her), and said, “O Mother of the Believers! Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to us a hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that if it is correct, then we are all doomed.” She said, “Whoever is destroyed by the saying of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he is truly destroyed. Tell me, what is that (hadith)?” I said, “The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Whoever wishes to meet Allah, Allah also wishes to meet him, and whoever does not wish to meet Allah, Allah does not wish to meet him. And there is none among us who does not dislike death.” Mother of the Believers, Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her), said: Indeed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said this, but it does not mean what you think. Rather, when the eyes turn (upwards), and the soul is held in the chest, and the hair stands on end on the body, and the fingers become contracted (i.e., in the state of death), then at that time, whoever wishes to meet Allah, Allah also wishes to meet him, and whoever dislikes to meet Allah, Allah also dislikes to meet him."
"455","Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say one day before his death: ""None of you should die except while having good expectations from Allah (that is, at the time of death, do not despair of Allah’s mercy, but rather hope for the grace and kindness of your Lord, and expect salvation and forgiveness from Him)."""
"456","Umm al-Mu’minin Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came to visit Abu Salamah (may Allah be pleased with him) when his eyes had become fixed (i.e., he had passed away). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) closed his eyes and said: “When the soul is taken away, the eyes follow it.” The people from his household began to weep, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Pray only for good for yourselves, for the angels say ‘Ameen’ to what you say.” Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) prayed: “O Allah! Forgive Abu Salamah (may Allah be pleased with him), raise his rank among those who are rightly guided, be the guardian of his family who remain, make his grave spacious and full of light for him. O Lord of all the worlds! Forgive us and forgive him.”"
"457","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) passed away, a Yemeni cloak was placed over him."
"458","`Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) (narrating from the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him) says that` when the soul of a believer departs from the body, two angels come before it and take it up to the sky. Hammad (the narrator of the hadith) said that Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) also mentioned the fragrance of that soul and musk, and said that the inhabitants of the heavens (the angels) say: ""A pure soul has come from the earth. May Allah have mercy on you and on your body which you inhabited."" Then they take it to the Lord of the worlds. Then the Lord of the worlds says: ""Take it (to its place, i.e., in 'Illiyyin where the souls of the believers reside) and keep it there until the Day of Resurrection."" And when the soul of a disbeliever departs (the narrator of the hadith) Hammad said that Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) mentioned its foul odor and the curse upon it, that the inhabitants of the heavens say: ""An impure soul has come from the earth."" Then the command is given: ""Take it (to its place in Sijjin where the souls of the disbelievers reside) until the Day of Resurrection."" Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), when mentioning the soul of the disbeliever and describing its foul odor, placed a fine cloth which he was wearing over his nose to demonstrate, and said: ""Like this."""
"459","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a woman who was weeping over her (deceased) child. So the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Fear Allah and be patient. The woman replied: What do you know of my calamity? When the Prophet (peace be upon him) left, it was said to the woman: Indeed, that was the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him). Then grief struck her like death. So the woman came to the door of the Prophet (peace be upon him) and found no doorkeeper at his door. She said: O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), I did not recognize you. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Indeed, patience is at the first stroke of calamity. (The narrator is in doubt whether the Prophet (peace be upon him) said ""at the first stroke of calamity"" or ""at the very first stroke of calamity."")"
"460","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said to the women of the Ansar: ""Whichever of you has three sons who die, and she (the woman) remains patient for the sake of Allah's pleasure, she will enter Paradise."" A woman asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! What if two children die?"" He, peace and blessings be upon him, replied, ""Even two."" In another chain of narration, it is reported in a marfu‘ form that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""A Muslim whose three children die will not be touched by the fire of Hell, except to fulfill an oath (that is, Allah the Exalted has said: 'There is none among you but will pass over it [Hell],' so he will pass over Hell, but will not be punished in any other way)."""
"461","Umm al-Mu’minin Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) says: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) saying that he (peace and blessings be upon him) used to say: When any servant is afflicted with a calamity and he recites this supplication: “Inna lillahi wa inna ilayhi raji’un... Allahumma’jurni fi musibati wakhluf li khayran minha” — that is, “Indeed, we belong to Allah and indeed, to Him we shall return. O Allah, reward me for my affliction and grant me something better than it in exchange.” (By reciting this supplication) Allah Almighty grants him reward for that calamity and gives him something better than what was lost. Umm al-Mu’minin Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) says: When (my first husband, Sayyiduna) Abu Salamah (may Allah be pleased with him) passed away, I recited (the mentioned supplication) as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had instructed me, so (by the blessing of this supplication) Allah Almighty granted me a better husband (that is, Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him) than my previous husband."
"462","‘Abdullah bin ‘Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) narrates that Sa‘d bin ‘Ubadah (may Allah be pleased with him) fell ill, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came to visit him, and ‘Abdur Rahman bin ‘Awf, Sa‘d, and ‘Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them) were with him. When he (peace and blessings be upon him) came to him, he found him unconscious, so he (peace and blessings be upon him) asked, “Has he passed away?” The people replied, “No.” Then he (peace and blessings be upon him) began to weep. When the people saw him (peace and blessings be upon him) weeping, they all began to weep. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “Listen, Allah does not punish for the tears of the eyes or the grief of the heart, but He punishes or shows mercy because of this”—and he (peace and blessings be upon him) pointed to his tongue—“that is, if a good word comes out of it, He shows mercy, and if an evil word comes out of it, He punishes.”"
"463","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Malik Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There are four things from the era of ignorance (i.e., the time of disbelief) in my Ummah that people will not abandon: boasting about one's lineage, defaming others' ancestry, seeking rain through the stars, and wailing (lamenting loudly) over the dead. And the woman who wails, if she does not repent before her death, then on the Day of Resurrection she will be clothed with a garment of sulphur and scabies."
"464","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not one of us who strikes his cheeks, tears his collar, or speaks the words of the days of ignorance (disbelief). In another narration, the word ""or"" is replaced with ""and""."
"465","´Sayyida Amrah bint Abdur Rahman (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that she heard from Ummul Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) (and in her presence it was mentioned that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) says that the dead is punished because of the weeping of the living over him), so Ummul Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) said: May Allah forgive Abu Abdur Rahman (may Allah be pleased with him), he did not lie but he made a mistake. The reality is that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) passed by a Jewish woman over whom people were weeping, so he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: They are weeping over her, while she is being punished in her grave."
"466","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah bin Rabi’i, may Allah be pleased with him, that a funeral passed by the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, and he said: ""One who has found relief, and others have found relief from him."" The people asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! What is the meaning of 'one who has found relief and others have found relief from him'?"" He, peace and blessings be upon him, replied: ""A believer finds relief from the hardships of the world (i.e., at the time of death), and from the departure of a wicked person, the servants, the city, the trees, and the animals find relief."""
"467","Lady Umm Atiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that when the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), Lady Zainab (may Allah be pleased with her), passed away, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) instructed us to wash her an odd number of times, three or five times. And on the fifth time, to use camphor or (he said) a little bit of camphor."
"468","Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was shrouded in three white sheets made of Sahul cotton. There was neither a shirt nor a turban among them, and people had a doubt about the Hullah. The reality is that the Hullah was bought for the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) so that he might be shrouded in it, but then it was not used, and he was shrouded in three sheets made of white Sahul. And Abdullah bin Abi Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) took the Hullah and said, “I will keep it and I will use it as my own shroud.” Then he said, “If Allah had liked it, it would have been used for the shroud of His Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him),” so he sold it and gave its price in charity."
"469","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, delivered a sermon one day and mentioned one of his companions who had passed away. He had been given a shroud that did not cover his private parts, and he was buried at night. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, expressed displeasure at his being buried at night, as he, peace and blessings be upon him, had not performed his funeral prayer. However, when a person is compelled (by necessity), it is excused. And the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: When any of you gives a shroud to his brother, he should give a good shroud (so that it covers his entire body well)."
"470","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Hasten with the funeral procession. For if the deceased was righteous, you are taking him towards goodness, and if he was evil, you are removing an evil from your necks."
"471","Lady Umm Atiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: We were forbidden to follow the funeral procession, but not emphatically."
"472","Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports: A funeral passed by and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) stood up, so we also stood up with him. Then we said, ""O Messenger of Allah! It is the funeral of a Jewish woman."" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Death is a distressing thing. When you see a funeral, stand up."""
"473","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: We saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) standing, so we also stood with him, and when he began to sit, we also began to sit, that is, during the funeral."
"474","`Sayyiduna Samurah bin Jundub (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` I offered the funeral prayer behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for the mother of Sayyiduna Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him), who had died during postpartum bleeding, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood at the middle of her body during the funeral prayer."
"475","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, informed (the companions) of the death of Najashi on the day he passed away. He went out with the companions to the prayer ground and offered four takbirs (in the funeral prayer) for him."
"476","Sayyiduna Abdur Rahman bin Abi Laila says that Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him) used to say four takbirs in our funeral prayers, and once he said five takbirs over a funeral. So I asked him, and he said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) (would also sometimes say five takbirs)."
"477","Sayyiduna Awf bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) offered the funeral prayer over a deceased person, and I remembered these words from his supplication: ""O Allah! Forgive him, have mercy on him, grant him well-being, pardon him, show him kindness through Your grace, make his home (grave) spacious, wash him with water, snow, and hail, cleanse him of sins as a white garment is cleansed of dirt, give him a home better than his home, people better than his people, a wife better than his wife, admit him to Paradise, and protect him from the punishment of the grave."" To the extent that I wished I were the deceased."
"478","Narrated from Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that when (the conqueror of Persia) Sayyiduna Sa’d bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him) passed away, the pure wives of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sent word asking that his funeral be brought through the mosque so that they could also offer the funeral prayer. So it was done as they requested. The bier was placed in front of their chambers so that they could pray, and then the funeral was taken out through the Gate of Funerals, which was towards Maqa’id. When people heard of this, they began to criticize and said, “Is a funeral ever brought into the mosque?” Upon this, Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) said, “How quick people are to criticize something about which they have no knowledge! They criticized us for bringing the funeral into the mosque, whereas the fact is that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) offered the funeral prayer for Suhail, the son of Bayda’, inside the mosque itself.”"
"479","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that there was an Abyssinian woman who used to clean the mosque, or it was a young man, and regarding him the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) inquired. The people replied that he had died. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Why did you not inform me?"" It was as if they considered him insignificant and did not want to trouble the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Show me his grave."" The people showed it to him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) offered prayer over it and said: ""These graves are filled with darkness, and Allah, because of my prayer, illuminates them for their inhabitants."""
"480","'Sayyiduna Jabir bin Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that a man (his funeral) was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who had killed himself with a broad arrow. So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) did not offer his funeral prayer.'"
"481","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Whoever attends a funeral until the prayer is offered (and participates in it), he will have a reward of one qirat, and whoever remains present until the burial, he will have a reward of two qirats. The companions asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! What is the meaning of two qirats?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: Like two great mountains in reward."
"482","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: There is no deceased person upon whom a group of Muslims, whose number reaches one hundred, offers the funeral prayer and then all intercede for him (that is, pray to Allah for his forgiveness), except that their intercession will be accepted."
"483","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that one of his sons died at (the place of) Qudayd or ‘Usfan. So he said (to his servant), ""O Kurayb! See how many people have gathered (for the funeral prayer)?"" Kurayb said, ""I went and saw that people had gathered, so I informed him."" Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said, ""In your estimation, are they forty?"" I said, ""Yes."" He said, ""Bring out the bier, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: 'Whenever forty people who do not associate anything with Allah attend the funeral of a Muslim, Allah certainly accepts their intercession for him.'"""
"484","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) reports: A funeral passed by and the people spoke well of it, so the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""It has become obligatory,"" three times he said this. Then another funeral passed by and the people spoke ill of it. The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""It has become obligatory,"" three times he said this. Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) submitted, ""May my parents be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of Allah! A funeral passed by and the people spoke well of it, and you said three times, 'It has become obligatory.' Then another passed by and the people spoke ill of it, and you said three times, 'It has become obligatory.' What does this mean (what has become obligatory)?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""For the one whom you spoke well of, Paradise has become obligatory, and for the one whom you spoke ill of, Hell has become obligatory. You are Allah’s witnesses on earth, you are Allah’s witnesses on earth, you are Allah’s witnesses on earth."""
"485","Jabir bin Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) offered the funeral prayer of Ibn Dahdah. Then a horse with a bare back (without a saddle) was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). A man held it, then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) mounted it, and it was jumping, and all of us were behind the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and running. So a man from the people said that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""How many clusters are hanging in Paradise for Ibn Dahdah."""
"486","`Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) says that` a red sheet was spread in the blessed grave of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)."
"487","'Amir bin Sa'd narrates that (the conqueror of Persia, Sayyiduna) Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him) said during his illness in which he passed away: ""Make a lahd (niche in the grave) for me and place unbaked bricks over it, just as was done for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)."""
"488","Abu al-Hayyaj al-Asadi says: Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said to me, ""I am sending you for the same task for which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sent me: that you erase every image and level every elevated grave to the ground."""
"489","'Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that' the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade plastering graves, sitting on them (using them as a place to rest), and constructing buildings (such as domes, etc.) over them."
"490","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: When any one of you dies, his abode is presented before him morning and evening. If he is among the people of Paradise, then (he is shown) among the people of Paradise, and if he is among the people of Hell, then (he is shown) among the people of Hell. Then it is said: This is your abode, until Allah sends you to it on the Day of Resurrection."
"491","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a servant is placed in his grave and his companions turn away and leave, he hears the sound of their footsteps. Then two angels come to him and say to him: What did you use to say about this man? (i.e., about Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him; his name is not mentioned with reverence here so that he does not understand.) The believer says: I bear witness that he is the servant of Allah and His Messenger. (May Allah’s mercy and peace be upon him.) Then it is said to him: Look at your place in the Hellfire; Allah has given you a place in Paradise instead of it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He sees both his places. Qatadah said that Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) mentioned to us that his grave is made seventy cubits wide and is filled with greenery (i.e., it becomes a garden) and will remain so until the Day of Resurrection."
"492","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Bara’ bin Azib, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: This verse, “Allah keeps firm those who believe with the firm word,” was revealed regarding the punishment of the grave. The deceased is asked, “Who is your Lord?” He says, “My Lord is Allah, and my Prophet is Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him.” This is what is meant by Allah’s statement, “Allah keeps firm those who believe with the firm word in this world and in the Hereafter.”"
"493","Narrated from Sayyiduna Bara’ bin Azib (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was going through the garden of Banu Najjar on his mule and we were with him. Suddenly, the mule shied and was about to throw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) off. There were six, or five, or four graves there. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked, “Does anyone know whose graves these are?” A man replied, “I know.” The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked, “When did these people die?” The man replied, “In the time of shirk (polytheism).” The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “The trial of this Ummah is in the graves. If you were not to stop burying your dead, I would have prayed to Allah to let you hear the punishment of the grave, which I am hearing.” Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned towards us and said, “Seek refuge with Allah from the punishment of Hell.” The people said, “We seek refuge with Allah from the punishment of Hell.” Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Seek refuge with Allah from the punishment of the grave.” The people said, “We seek refuge with Allah from the punishment of the grave.” The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Seek refuge with Allah from the trials, both hidden and open.” The people said, “We seek refuge with Allah from the trials, both hidden and open.” The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Seek refuge with Allah from the trial of Dajjal.” The people said, “We seek refuge with Allah from the trial of Dajjal.”"
"494","`Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) heard a sound after the sun had set, so he said that the Jews are being punished in their graves."
"495","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) visited his mother’s grave, and he (peace be upon him) wept, causing those around him to weep as well. Then he (peace be upon him) said: I sought permission from my Lord to seek forgiveness for my mother, but I was not granted permission. And I sought permission to visit her grave, and I was granted permission. Therefore, visit graves, for they remind you of death."
"496","Sayyiduna Buraidah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: I used to forbid you from visiting graves, but now you should visit them. And I used to forbid you from keeping the meat of sacrifice for more than three days, but now keep it as long as you wish. And I used to forbid you from drinking nabidh (fermented drink) in containers other than water skins, but now drink from any drinking vessel you wish, but do not drink anything intoxicating."
"497","Muhammad bin Qais said one day, ""Shall I not tell you something about myself and my mother?"" We thought that perhaps by 'mother' he meant the one who gave birth to him. Then he said, ""Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) said: Shall I not tell you something about myself and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)?"" We said, ""Certainly."" She said: ""One night the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was with me. He turned over, put aside his cloak, took off his shoes and placed them in front of his feet, spread the edge of his cloak on his bedding, and lay down. He stayed for a short while, thinking that I had fallen asleep. Then, quietly, he took his cloak, quietly put on his shoes, quietly opened the door, went out, and quietly closed it. I also took my cloak, covered my head, veiled myself, and followed the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) until he reached Baqi' and stood there for a long time. Then he raised both hands three times, and then returned, so I also returned. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) walked quickly, so I walked quickly. He ran, so I ran. He came home, so I also came home, but I arrived before him and lay down as soon as I entered. When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) entered the house, he said, 'O Aisha! What has happened to you that you are out of breath and your belly is heaving?' I said, 'Nothing.' He said, 'Tell me, otherwise the All-Aware, the All-Knowing (meaning Allah Almighty) will inform me.' I said, 'May my parents be sacrificed for you.' Then I informed him (i.e., told him the whole story). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, 'The shadow I saw ahead of me was you?' I said, 'Yes.' So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) struck me on the chest (this was out of affection) so that I felt pain, and said, 'Did you think that Allah and His Messenger would wrong you? (Meaning, that I would go to another wife during your turn?)' I said, 'When people hide something, Allah knows it.' (Meaning, even if you had gone to another wife, Allah would have seen it.) The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, 'Jibreel (peace be upon him) came to me when you saw me get up. He called me and concealed himself from you, so I also wanted to conceal it from you. He did not come to you because you had taken off your extra garment (for sleep), and I thought you had fallen asleep, so I disliked waking you and also feared that you would be alarmed as to where I had gone.' Then Jibreel (peace be upon him) said, 'Your Lord commands you to go to Baqi' and seek forgiveness for the people of Baqi'.' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah! How should I say it?' The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, 'Say: Peace be upon the people of Islam and the believing inhabitants (of these graves), and may Allah have mercy on those who have gone ahead of us and those who come later, and if Allah wills, we too shall join you (after death).'"""
"498","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: If someone were to sit on a burning ember that burns his clothes and reaches his skin, it would still be better than sitting on a grave (i.e., keeping vigil there)."
"499","Sayyiduna Abu Marthad Ghanawi (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Do not sit on the grave and do not pray towards it."
"500","Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was asked: ""What do you say about a person who does good deeds and people praise him for it?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: ""This is an immediate glad tiding for the believer (i.e., the reward and recompense in the Hereafter is separate; this is a source of happiness for him in this world that people praise him)."""
